      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your parents' reaction is not a judgment of your worth, but a reflection of their own deep confusion and fear of losing the only person they knew. The idea that you are a burden is a lie you tell yourself to protect yourself from the truth that you are still loved, even if you can't see it. You are not a mistake; you are a human being who has finally stopped performing, and that is a terrifying but necessary step toward becoming who you truly are.",
